STUDENT PROJECT CATALOG PORTAL

USER STORIES AND ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

1. USER STORIES OVERVIEW

Format: As a [role], I want [goal], so that [benefit].

Students act in two modes:

1. Seeker: Browses and requests projects.
2. Contributor: Posts their own projects.

Acceptance criteria (AC) are provided for key user stories.

2. STUDENT STORIES

All stories below begin with "As a student" unless the role is stated.

EPIC 1: ACCOUNT AND AUTHENTICATION

S1 - User Registration

User Story:
As a visitor, I want to register with name, email and password, so that I can request or post projects.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Email must be unique.
- Password must be hashed.
- New accounts must receive the Student role.

S2 - User Login

User Story:
I want to log in, so that I can access my dashboard.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Wrong credentials must show a clear error.
- Repeated login failures must be rate-limited.

S3 - User Logout

User Story:
I want to log out, so that my account stays safe on shared computers.

S4 - Password Reset

User Story:
I want to reset a forgotten password by email, so that I am never locked out.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Reset link must expire quickly.
- Reset link must work only once.

S5 - Protected Pages

User Story:
I want protected pages to redirect me to login when signed out, so that my data stays private.

EPIC 2: BROWSING AND DISCOVERY

S6 - Project Catalog Display

User Story:
As a visitor, I want a grid of cards showing image, title, course, technology, level, rating and an Official/Community badge, so that I can scan options and judge trust at a glance.

S7 - Keyword Search

User Story:
I want to search by keyword, so that I can find projects by name or topic.

S8 - Project Filtering

User Story:
I want to filter by course, technology, level and source, so that I see only relevant projects.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Filters must be combinable.

S9 - Project Sorting

User Story:
I want to sort by newest, top rated or title, so that I can prioritize.

S10 - Pagination and URL Filters

User Story:
I want paginated results with filters kept in the URL, so that browsing is fast and shareable.

Acceptance Criteria:
- List endpoints must respond in under 500 ms.

S11 - Project Detail Page

User Story:
I want a detail page with description, screenshots, tech stack, what is included and how to run, so that I can decide before requesting.

S12 - Community Project Author Details

User Story:
I want to see the author's name and profile on community projects, so that I know who built it.

S13 - Project Reviews

User Story:
I want to read reviews from other students, so that I can judge quality.

S14 - Empty States

User Story:
I want friendly empty states when nothing matches, so that I know what to try next.

EPIC 3: REQUESTING AND DOWNLOADING

S15 - Request a Project

User Story:
I want to send a request with a short note, so that the approver has context.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Only logged-in students can request projects.
- No duplicate active request is allowed for the same project.
- Students cannot request their own projects.

S16 - Track Request Status

User Story:
I want to see request status (Pending, Approved, Rejected, Delivered), so that I know where it stands.

S17 - Request Status Email Notifications

User Story:
I want an email on every status change, so that I do not have to keep checking.

S18 - View Rejection Reason

User Story:
I want to read the rejection reason, so that I understand the decision.

S19 - Approval-Based Download Access

User Story:
I want a download button that appears only after approval, so that I get files only when entitled.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Download button must remain hidden before approval.
- Downloads must be blocked by the API before approval.
- Download links must expire shortly.
- A fresh link can be generated from the dashboard.

S20 - One-Click ZIP Download

User Story:
I want one-click ZIP download, so that I can start right away.

EPIC 4: CONTRIBUTING PROJECTS

S21 - Accept Project Posting Rules

User Story:
I want to read the posting rules and accept a terms agreement before submitting, so that I understand my responsibilities.

Acceptance Criteria:
- The student must confirm that the work is their own or they have the right to share it.

S22 - Submit a Community Project

User Story:
I want a "Submit a project" form (title, course, tech stack, level, description, how-to-run, screenshots, ZIP), so that my project is complete.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Incomplete submissions cannot be sent.
- Only allowed file types and sizes are accepted.

S23 - Save Submission as Draft

User Story:
I want to save a submission as a draft, so that I can finish it later.

S24 - Track Submission Status

User Story:
I want to see my submission status (Draft, Pending Review, Approved, Rejected, Changes Requested), so that I know what is next.

S25 - View Admin Feedback

User Story:
I want to read admin feedback when my submission is rejected or needs changes, so that I can fix and resubmit.

S26 - Submission Status Email Notifications

User Story:
I want an email when my submission's status changes, so that I am informed immediately.

S27 - Edit Published Project

User Story:
I want to edit my published project, so that I can improve or fix it.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Significant edits must send the project back for re-review.

S28 - Withdraw or Delete Own Project

User Story:
I want to withdraw or delete my own project, so that I control my work.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Past requests and downloads must not be broken.

S29 - Public Author Profile

User Story:
I want a public author profile listing my published projects and average rating, so that I get recognition.

S30 - View Project Requests and Downloads

User Story:
I want to see requests and downloads my projects received, so that I know they are useful.

EPIC 5: DASHBOARD AND PROFILE

S31 - My Requests

User Story:
I want "My Requests", so that I can track everything in one place.

S32 - My Downloads

User Story:
I want "My Downloads", so that I can find projects I received.

S33 - My Submissions

User Story:
I want "My Submissions", so that I can manage what I posted.

S34 - Edit Profile and Change Password

User Story:
I want to edit my profile and change my password, so that my account stays current and secure.

EPIC 6: REVIEWS AND REPORTING

S35 - Rate and Review a Project

User Story:
I want to rate (1 to 5) and review a project after downloading it, so that I help others choose.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Only students who downloaded the project can review it.
- One review per project per student.
- Students cannot review their own projects.

S36 - Edit or Delete Own Review

User Story:
I want to edit or delete my own review, so that I can correct mistakes.

S37 - Report Inappropriate Content

User Story:
I want to report a project or review that breaks the rules, so that quality stays high.

STUDENT STRETCH STORIES

S38 - Wishlist

User Story:
I want a wishlist to save projects for later.

S39 - Request Chat

User Story:
I want a chat thread on a request to ask questions without email.

3. ADMIN STORIES

All stories below begin with "As an admin".

EPIC 7: ACCESS AND SECURITY

A1 - Role-Protected Admin Panel

User Story:
I want a role-protected admin panel, so that only authorized people manage the system.

Acceptance Criteria:
- A student calling an admin endpoint must receive HTTP 403 Forbidden.

A2 - Secure Token-Based Sessions

User Story:
I want secure token-based sessions, so that my powerful account is harder to hijack.

EPIC 8: OFFICIAL CATALOG MANAGEMENT

A3 - Create Official Projects

User Story:
I want to create official projects with full details, screenshots and ZIP, so that the catalog has a trusted baseline.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Official projects must be published immediately with the Official badge.

A4 - Edit Official Projects

User Story:
I want to edit official projects, so that I can fix errors or update files.

A5 - Delete or Deactivate Projects

User Story:
I want to delete or deactivate any project (isActive), so that outdated or problematic ones disappear without breaking past requests.

A6 - Searchable and Filterable Project Management

User Story:
I want a searchable, filterable list of all projects (any source or status), so that I can manage a large catalog.

A7 - Enforce Upload Restrictions

User Story:
I want upload type and size limits enforced, so that bad files never enter storage.

EPIC 9: COMMUNITY SUBMISSION REVIEW

A8 - Pending Submission Review Queue

User Story:
I want a review queue of pending student submissions, so that nothing goes live unchecked.

A9 - Preview Community Submissions

User Story:
I want to preview a submission's details, screenshots and ZIP, so that I can check it against the rules.

A10 - Approve Community Submissions

User Story:
I want to approve a submission, so that it goes live with the Community badge.

Acceptance Criteria:
- The author must receive an email.
- The project must appear in the catalog.

A11 - Reject Community Submissions

User Story:
I want to reject a submission with a required reason, so that the student understands.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Rejection must be blocked if the reason is empty.

A12 - Request Changes to Submissions

User Story:
I want to request changes with specific notes, so that the student can improve and resubmit.

A13 - Unpublish Community Projects

User Story:
I want to unpublish any community project later, so that I can act on problems found after approval.

A14 - Handle Student Reports

User Story:
I want to handle student reports on projects and reviews, so that rule-breaking content is removed.

A15 - Warn or Ban Students

User Story:
I want to warn or ban a student from posting after repeated violations, so that the community stays healthy.

EPIC 10: REQUEST REVIEW

A16 - View All Project Requests

User Story:
I want to see all requests with student, project, note, status and date, so that I can review efficiently.

A17 - Filter Project Requests

User Story:
I want to filter requests by status and project source, so that I can focus on what needs action.

A18 - Approve Project Requests

User Story:
I want to approve a request, so that the student can download.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Request status must change.
- An email must be sent.
- Download access must be unlocked.

A19 - Reject Project Requests

User Story:
I want to reject a request with a required reason, so that the student understands.

Acceptance Criteria:
- An email containing the rejection reason must be sent.

A20 - Mark Requests as Delivered

User Story:
I want requests marked Delivered after download, so that I can tell fulfilled from open ones.

EPIC 11: USERS AND INSIGHTS

A21 - User Management

User Story:
I want a user list with role, join date and posting status, so that I can see who uses the portal.

A22 - Platform Statistics

User Story:
I want a stats page (projects official vs community, submissions by status, requests by status, top courses and contributors), so that I can see demand and activity.

A23 - Moderate Reviews

User Story:
I want to moderate reviews, so that ratings stay trustworthy.

ADMIN STRETCH STORIES

A24 - CSV Export

User Story:
I want CSV export of requests and submissions.

A25 - Request Chat Replies

User Story:
I want to reply in request chat threads.

A26 - Delegate Request Approval

User Story:
I want to delegate request approval for a community project to its author.

4. SYSTEM AND QUALITY STORIES

Q1 - Performance

Requirement:
List endpoints respond in under 500 ms.

Q2 - Authentication and Input Security

Requirement:
Login attempts are rate-limited and all inputs sanitized.

Q3 - File Upload Security

Requirement:
Uploads are restricted by type and size, and checked where possible.

Q4 - Download Security

Requirement:
Download links expire after a short time.

Q5 - Role and Ownership Authorization

Requirement:
Role and ownership checks are enforced in the API (for example, a student can edit only their own project).

Q6 - Public Project Visibility

Requirement:
Only approved, active projects appear in public listings.

Q7 - Automated Testing

Requirement:
Jest and Supertest API tests plus one Playwright end-to-end test cover the full flow: submit, review, request, approve, download.

5. PRIORITY CLASSIFICATION

MUST-HAVE REQUIREMENTS

- Student stories: S1 to S37.
- Admin stories: A1 to A23.
- System and quality requirements: Q1 to Q7.

STRETCH (BONUS) REQUIREMENTS

- S38: Wishlist.
- S39: Request chat.
- A24: CSV export of requests and submissions.
- A25: Reply in request chat threads.
- A26: Delegate request approval for a community project to its author.

6. FEATURES THAT CAN BE DEFERRED

If the project scope becomes too large for 12 weeks, the safest items to defer are:

- S29: Author profile.
- S30: Project request and download statistics for authors.
- A15: Ban system.
- S37: Reporting projects or reviews.
- A14: Admin handling of reports.

